From: adb-rt (armv7-pc-windows-msvc port)
Subject: [PATCH] adb: use string_view::data() with std::from_chars, not begin()/end()

*** UPSTREAMABLE TO AOSP. This is a genuine portability fix, not a local workaround. ***

ParseUint() calls std::from_chars(str.begin(), str.end(), value) on a std::string_view.
That only compiles because libc++ and libstdc++ HAPPEN to define
std::string_view::const_iterator as a bare `const char*`. The C++ standard leaves that type
IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED ([string.view.template] - it need only be a random-access iterator),
so the current code relies on unspecified behaviour.

The MSVC STL defines it as a checked class, `std::_String_view_iterator<char_traits<char>>`.
std::from_chars takes `const char*`, so on MSVC the call does not compile:

  adb_utils.h(114): error: no matching function for call to 'from_chars'
    note: candidate function not viable: no known conversion from 'const_iterator'
          (aka '_String_view_iterator<std::char_traits<char>>') to 'const char *const'

str.data() and str.data() + str.size() are the portable spelling, are exactly equivalent on
libc++/libstdc++, and are what from_chars actually wants. Three sites in one function:

  114  the from_chars() call itself
  118  comparing res.ptr (const char*) against str.end()
  122  str.end() - res.ptr  -> invalid operands (const_iterator and const char* const)

Note: three lines, not two. 118 and 122 fail for the same reason as 114 and are only
reachable once 114 is fixed, so they surface one at a time.

No behavioural change on any toolchain.

Measured on: clang 23.1.1-rt2, --target=thumbv7-unknown-windows-msvc, MSVC 14.44.35207 STL.
Fixes compilation of sockets.cpp and client/transport_local.cpp.
---
--- a/adb_utils.h
+++ b/adb_utils.h
@@ -111,15 +111,15 @@
 template <typename T>
 inline bool ParseUint(T* result, std::string_view str, std::string_view* remaining = nullptr) {
     T value;
-    const auto res = std::from_chars(str.begin(), str.end(), value);
+    const auto res = std::from_chars(str.data(), str.data() + str.size(), value);
     if (res.ec != std::errc{}) {
         return false;
     }
-    if (res.ptr != str.end() && !remaining) {
+    if (res.ptr != str.data() + str.size() && !remaining) {
         return false;
     }
     if (remaining) {
-        *remaining = std::string_view(res.ptr, str.end() - res.ptr);
+        *remaining = std::string_view(res.ptr, str.data() + str.size() - res.ptr);
     }
     *result = value;
     return true;
